                <pb facs="0244" n="154" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg154"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1753</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-05-07T15:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 7, 1918, 3
                                p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 7, 2.50 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your May 1, 5 p.m. My telegrams April 25, 5 p.m.,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d202-f1"/>
                    April 27, 1 p.m.,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d202-f2"/> April 30, 2 p.m.,<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d202-f3"/> give the information available. The movement, <pb
                        facs="0245" n="155" xml:id="pg155"/> avowedly administrative, is believed to
                    be primarily political and to aim at constituting a government for Siberia with
                    the same personnel after military success achieved with assistance from Allies
                    or Japanese alone.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
